#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078129 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "98fdea06-a5ad-5d22-b928-ef893424e447" :question/math-academy-id "e-158" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.2$. We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1$. This gives\n\n$$\nf^{′}(0.2) \\mid \\approx (f(0.2 + 0.1) - f(0.2 - 0.1))/(2(0.1)); = (f(0.3) - f(0.1))/(2(0.1)); = \\frac{1.7 - 1.1}{0.2}; = \\frac{0.6}{0.2}; = \\frac{6}{2}; = 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078130 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "62934fda-d972-50d5-acdb-e1f7b2fd63f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-159" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above.\nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/a750fcfca1b253b803c467e2619376fd.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4$. This gives\n\n$$\ng^{′}(4) \\mid \\approx (g(4 + 4) - g(4 - 4))/(2(4)); = (g(8) - g(0))/(8); = (-4 - (-10))/(8); = \\frac{6}{8}; = 0.75\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078133 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "d405fda1-1111-56db-ae34-4c0f257852f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-160" :question/problem "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}$. The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t)$. The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/2189fc374802d088f3c8ca4094372036.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1$." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1$. This gives\n\n$$\nT^{′}(3) \\mid \\approx (T(3 + 1) - T(3 - 1))/(2(1)); = (T(4) - T(2))/(2); = \\frac{60 - 30}{2}; = \\frac{30}{2}; = 15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7b839a2-a641-5253-802a-0d8e3959e566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075915} {:answer/id #uuid "c483963e-57f9-5d4e-9222-ae0776f9ac4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075916} {:answer/id #uuid "1147e451-0584-572f-ad2b-ced4053053f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075917} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9de122-54df-5942-ad79-cbc266f5a635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075918} {:answer/id #uuid "7fef81f0-ea59-50f8-a66b-0437137410e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c483963e-57f9-5d4e-9222-ae0776f9ac4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "g^{′}(-1) \\approx - 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3519576-a94b-5410-8340-1c167b379854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075914}] :question/id #uuid "db9edec3-4494-5ddd-9ed4-509fa1e568a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32535" :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\nApproximate $g^{′}(x)$ at the point $x =-1$ using a central difference approximation." :question/requires-calculator true}]}
